# Notification and progress isolation contract (#1002).
# Supply a real access token and internal organization GUID. UserId, when supplied,
# is only an assertion of the authenticated oid; it never selects another user.
# Lists/counts/read mutations include only the actor's system-visible notifications.
# Cross-actor, foreign-tenant or inaccessible IDs in mark-read reject the entire batch.
# Ordinary mode ignores support cookies. Explicit support requires a matching live session.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@token = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
@tenantId = REPLACE_WITH_INTERNAL_ORGANIZATION_GUID
@notificationId = REPLACE_WITH_AUTHORIZED_NOTIFICATION_GUID

### Transport capabilities (also usable with an existing server-authenticated session)
# Missing bearer credentials do not enable cookie-based SignalR. The response exposes
# server-bound recipientId, REST availability, realtime availability/reason, and a polling
# recommendation. Frontends must not require an MSAL account merely to use authorized REST.
# To test an existing server-authenticated session without bearer, omit Authorization;
# do not manufacture cookies or identity headers. Anonymous requests remain 401.
# A session-only organization response has:
# rest.available=true; realtime.available=false; realtime.cookieSessionSupported=false;
# realtime.reasonCode=REALTIME_BEARER_REQUIRED;
# fallback.transport=rest-polling; fallback.pollIntervalSeconds=30.
# Other realtime reasons: REALTIME_BEARER_INVALID, REALTIME_ACTOR_MISMATCH,
# REALTIME_WORKSPACE_NOT_AUTHORIZED. Presence of an Authorization header alone is not readiness.
# Subscription/resource authorization still runs even when realtime.available=true.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/notifications/capabilities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### List visible notifications
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/notifications?unreadOnly=true&limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Visible summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/notifications/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Mark only authorized actor-owned notifications
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/notifications/mark-read
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"notificationIds":["{{notificationId}}"]}

### Mark all visible notifications; inaccessible systems remain unchanged
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/notifications/mark-all-read
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Actor and organization bound preferences
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/notifications/preferences
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Save preferences
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/notifications/preferences
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{"poamOverdueAlerts":true,"atoExpirationAlerts":true,"complianceDriftAlerts":true,"alertDaysBefore":30}

### A forged userId assertion must be forbidden, never another user's inbox
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/notifications?userId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

# SignalR transports: /hubs/notifications, /hubs/package, /hubs/import-progress.
# Append workspaceKind=organization&workspaceTenantId=<internal GUID>&workspaceMode=ordinary.
# Retain accessTokenFactory (negotiate bearer header, WS/SSE GET access_token).
# Reconnect on context changes. Package: SubscribeToPackage/UnsubscribeFromPackage(packageId).
# Import: JoinImportGroup/LeaveImportGroup(importJobId). Both IDs are server-created GUIDs.
# Each operation and progress delivery revalidates workspace membership and system read access.
# Job knowledge alone grants no access. Do not use ordinary contexts as support-session aliases.
#
# The import polling fallback applies identical workspace/system read checks. Upload and
# cancellation additionally require the shared CanRunAssessments permission.
@systemId = REPLACE_WITH_REGISTERED_SYSTEM_ID
@importId = REPLACE_WITH_IMPORT_JOB_GUID

### Import polling fallback (404 for inaccessible system/job)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/systems/{{systemId}}/scans/import/{{importId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary

### Cancel import (403 for read-only system assignees)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/systems/{{systemId}}/scans/import/{{importId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
